## What I did

`scripts/social.sh` (3 additive hunks, +74 lines, nothing removed):

1. `export YOYO_AUDIT=1 before the invocation, plus AUDIT_BEFORE` — the audit file's line count taken before the run.
2. A fail-soft report_social_spend() that reads the usage line out of $AGENT_LOG before it's deleted, and prints the per-run audit delta beside the cumulative byte size, separately labelled.
3. Called at both doors where $AGENT_LOG dies: the API-error early exit and the main path.

Why this and not a new feature: yoyo already prints the run's usage (print_usage → format_usage_line); social.sh:358 tee'd it into a mktemp file that :376 then rm -f'd unread. The spend was discarded by one rm — so the fix is a read.

## Verification (the dry-run is the real one; the cargo run is a tree regression check)

bash -n clean; cargo fmt --check, clippy -D warnings, build, test all green (17 result lines, 0 failures); the heredoc lint passes.

Six stub cases in throwaway mktemp -d dirs, against the accounting block sed-extracted from the script itself:

| case | result |
|---|---|
| usage present | Spend (this run): ↳ 4.2s · 100→20 tokens (5 tok/s) · $0.0010 + 2 record(s) this run (line 0 → 2); 199 bytes cumulative |
| usage absent (exit 124) | no usage record — the process did not reach its terminal emit (no_terminal_emit) — not `0` — delta still reported |
| no audit file | warning, exit 0, run continues |
| persistent checkout (5 pre-existing lines) | 2 record(s) this run (line 5 → 7) — the watermark doing its one job |
| API-error early exit | spend reported before rm |
| degenerate near-miss | both honest absences, exit 0 → additive, cannot break a real run |

Two claims I verified rather than trusted from the task file:

• **The Step 8 safety check cannot see the audit file.** All three probes (`ls-files --others --exclude-standard`, `diff --name-only`, `diff --cached --name-only`) return 0 lines for it, while the control `git ls-files --others (no --exclude-standard`) names it — so the file exists and is invisible to the revert. No exemption was needed.
• **The usage-line shape** was read out of `format_usage_line` at HEAD, not hand-written from the task file's memory, and the absent-line wording reuses `extract_trajectory.py`'s `USAGE_NO_TERMINAL_EMIT` rather than a second phrasing.

## Residue, stated plain

This is a per-run report, not a durable sink — a runner that's thrown away still loses it. The sink (which would live in social.yml, a human's file), the sub-agent token floor (yoagent#173, which makes any total here a floor), and the other three uninstrumented phases (dream.sh, daily_diary.sh, synthesize.yml) stay in #944. I copied the pattern to nothing else — one phase at a time, deliberately.

